session: retire retained conversations during deletion

Bind deletion preparation to the ordinary owner's persisted journal and
exact retained root. Preserve an attempted, unbootstrapped threadless
reservation as a removed tombstone when both initial-request flags are
explicitly false, keeping its project and native outcome unknown.

Check confirmed members before quiescence and publish tombstones only
after thread_retiring is durable. Ordinary archive and member retirement
keep their existing refusal and recovery behavior within schema 1.

For a positively proved root missing from the index, require its unique
loaded identity or positive persisted empty-preview, unloaded root proof.
Keep exact metadata and materialized file identity stable through history,
idle and resolved-submission checks. Preserve unrelated structured sources
and retain attempt evidence on failure.
